<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-9">9 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The House of Representatives elects John Quincy Adams president</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">No candidate had won a majority of the electoral vote in 1824, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a>, Adams, Henry Clay and William Crawford ran, so the House held a contingent election under the Twelfth Amendment. It chose Adams as the sixth president.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-12">12 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Creek cede their last Georgia lands at Indian Springs</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By the Treaty of Indian Springs, concluded with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a> (Creek) ceded the last of their lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> to the US government and migrated west. An additional article was added to the treaty two days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-5">5 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Spanish, Danish and US forces trap the pirate Roberto Cofresí</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the US <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Squadron and the Danish government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-thomas-u-s-virgin-islands">Saint Thomas</a> forced Cofresí's sloop Anne into a 45-minute battle. He escaped overland but was ambushed and captured, and on 29 March he was executed by firing squad in San Juan.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-6">6 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bolivia declares independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sucre">Chuquisaca</a> proclaimed the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a>, naming the new republic after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-jose-de-sucre">Antonio José de Sucre</a> became its first president.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-25">25 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Uruguay declares independence from Brazil</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A congress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> declared the Banda Oriental independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Empire of Brazil</a> and united with the River Plate provinces. After a war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> became a sovereign state under the 1828 treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-27">27 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Stockton and Darlington Railway opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">George Stephenson drove Locomotion No. 1, hauling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> wagons and hundreds of passengers, on the opening run. It was the world's first public railway to use <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steam-locomotive">steam locomotives</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-26">26 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Erie Canal opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor DeWitt Clinton set off from Buffalo on the newly completed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erie-canal">Erie Canal</a>, which linked Lake Erie to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson River</a> over 363 miles. Cheap transport to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midwestern-united-states">Midwest</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City the nation's leading port.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-26">26 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Decembrist revolt fails in St Petersburg</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers led troops onto Senate Square to refuse allegiance to Nicholas I and demand reform. Cannon fire dispersed them; five leaders were hanged, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decembrists">Decembrists</a> inspired later Russian radicals.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/decembrists" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/decembrists.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/decembrists">Decembrists</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Decembrists were Russian army officers and nobles who staged a revolt in St Petersburg on 14 December 1825 (Old Style), refusing to swear allegiance to Nicholas I and seeking a constitution or a republic and the end of serfdom.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tumusla" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tumusla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tumusla">Battle of Tumusla</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tumusla was fought on 1 April 1825 in Upper Peru, present-day Bolivia, between the last royalist forces under Pedro Antonio Olañeta and troops who had turned against him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-danubyu" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-danubyu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-danubyu">Battle of Danubyu</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Danubyu was fought in March and April 1825 during the First Anglo-Burmese War, when a British force attacked the Burmese fortified position at Danubyu in the Irrawaddy delta.</p></div></li></ol></section>
