<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-haiti-1806-1849"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Haiti%20(1806-1849).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Haiti (1806-1849)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">France recognises Haiti in return for an indemnity of 150 million francs</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Bolivia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Bolivia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Upper Peru declares independence at Chuquisaca as the Republic of Bolívar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/decembrist-revolt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Decembrist%20revolt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Decembrist revolt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Alexander I dies suddenly, and parts of the army swear loyalty to Konstantin, unaware that he has renounced the throne</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/decembrist-revolt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Decembrist%20revolt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Decembrist revolt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">About 3,000 rebel troops refuse the oath to Nicholas I in Senate Square, Saint Petersburg, and are scattered by artillery</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-ayacucho"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Ayacucho.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Ayacucho</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Olañeta is killed at Tumusla and royalist resistance in Upper Peru ends</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-navarino"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Navarino.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Navarino</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ibrahim Pasha lands in the Peloponnese with 16,000 men and overruns its western part</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/saint-petersburg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saint%20Petersburg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saint Petersburg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Decembrist revolt takes place on Senate Square</span></li></ul></section>
